{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The J-B Weld epoxy fits my pattern of buying tape, vinyl cement, and fasteners for repairs, provided the repair calls for a rigid bond.",
    "The digital caliper would help me measure hose and fitting diameters before choosing clamps, so it connects directly to my repeated clamp purchases."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The filament recommendations depend on me using a 3D printer, which my purchases do not establish; buying repair supplies does not give me a reason to buy printing material.",
    "Different filament colors, finishes, and large quantities do not make them useful without a printing project. The infrared thermometer is more plausible for maintenance, but I still lack a specific temperature-measuring task."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in practical tools seems to have been stretched into an assumed interest in 3D printing.",
    "Materials used to make new objects seem to have been treated as interchangeable with supplies I use to repair or secure existing things."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated hose-clamp purchases suggest that fitting, sizing, and securing connections matter to me, which makes a measuring tool particularly relevant.",
    "I choose supplies for specific tasks: tape, vinyl cement, and electrical connectors each serve a purpose. A recommendation needs a similarly clear use before I would choose it."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognize my repair needs but assume a printing hobby that my purchases do not support."
}"}
